WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.320
4-100 GLP-1 stoppers had a heart event or died yearly, double those who continued in observational records. This is peptides weekly episode 9. Education and evidence never dosing advice. After that record study, a label warning on a rare eye event, then emergency room complications, then two clinic studies of tirzepatide and the peptide spotlight on dual agonists. People with type 2 diabetes and no-known heart disease were tracked in Italian clinic records.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:36.440
Global News and the South First Report across 301 clinics from 2004 through 2024.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:43.140
The analysis in the Lancet Regional Health Europe covered 80,302 people who had started

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.180
a GLP-1 receptor agonist.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:51.400
After matching on baseline traits, each side held 28,713 people.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:57.900
The combined rate of non-fatal heart attack, non-fatal stroke or death was 3.94 events

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:05.000
per 100 person years after a stop against 1.96 among people who continued, a hazard ratio

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:13.600
of 2.03, death from any cause was 2.23 versus 0.48 events per 100 person years, a hazard

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:21.300
ratio of 4.81, and the gap was wider when body mass index was 30 or higher, about 60% stopped

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.940
after roughly a year, while people who stayed on treatment did so for about 3 years.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:30.640
A British medical journal read of the same study said it could not show that stopping

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.580
caused the extra events because it never learned why people stopped.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.380
Gut side effects, cost, illness, and some may already have been sicker.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.760
Christopher Labos, a cardiologist and epidemiologist, told Global News the pattern fits a known

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.800
on-treatment heart benefit that you no longer get if the drug is gone.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:57.400
A separate BMJ review from January 2026, 63 trials and more than 9,000 people found

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:02.480
weight coming back at about 0.4 kilograms a month after weight loss drugs were stopped.

00:02:03.286 --> 00:02:07.946
The Food and Drug Administration, since the 5th of November, has added a warning rather

00:02:07.946 --> 00:02:08.926
than a new approval.

00:02:09.426 --> 00:02:14.966
Timeline Daily, with drug topics and R's Technica describing the same action, says labels

00:02:14.966 --> 00:02:20.606
minerals must now name non-artoridic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy, a rare sudden drop

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:25.846
in blood flow to the optic nerve. It can bring acute, painless loss of vision in one eye,

00:02:26.326 --> 00:02:32.486
and that loss can be permanent. The products named are ozempic, wagovi, mongaro, zepbound,

00:02:32.746 --> 00:02:38.566
and selicwa. Diabetes, smoking, high blood pressure, and high cholesterol are listed as risk

00:02:38.566 --> 00:02:43.966
factors for the eye condition itself. This is a regulatory labeling step, not a trial that

00:02:43.966 --> 00:02:48.686
that counted how often the event occurs, and it does not mean every vision change on treatment

00:02:48.686 --> 00:02:49.846
is this diagnosis.

00:02:50.943 --> 00:02:55.483
Emergency departments are the setting Miriam Fisher described to W-B-A-L-T-V.

00:02:56.083 --> 00:03:01.063
The MedStar Emergency Physician said patients come in every day with GLP1 side effects,

00:03:01.563 --> 00:03:06.263
and that more of those visits look preventable as people buy the drugs online and use them

00:03:06.263 --> 00:03:07.063
without a clinician.

00:03:07.823 --> 00:03:12.803
What she is seeing is not a tabulated study, vomiting so severe that food and drink will

00:03:12.803 --> 00:03:19.403
not stay down, dehydration, and then gall bladder and biliary disease, pancreatitis and kidney stones

00:03:19.403 --> 00:03:25.243
when dehydration is marked. She said these peptides slow the gut so a little nausea can be expected,

00:03:25.723 --> 00:03:31.163
and severe pain should not. Her view is that the medicines are useful and belong under a doctor's

00:03:31.163 --> 00:03:38.140
care. Lipidema symptom scores are the subject of a metabolism open paper on 49 women treated in

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:43.960
routine care at one specialist clinic from January 2024 to May 2026.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:49.340
Tears Epitide is approved for Type 2 diabetes in the United States, Europe, and the United

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:50.220
Arab Emirates.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:55.920
This series is not an approval study for lipidema, and it has no untreated comparison group.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:00.580
Investigators compared the lipidema symptom assessment questionnaire before treatment

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:03.120
with the latest score 3-18 months later.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:12.500
percentage symptom change did not track percentage weight change. The correlation was 0.058 and the p value was 0.692

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.600
and symptom change also failed to track dose intensity or how long treatment lasted.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:26.000
Weight change did track dose intensity and duration with correlations of minus 0.569 and minus 0.611.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:32.260
one. Every woman improved at least 30% on the questionnaire, and 93.9% improved at

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:37.460
least 50%. The authors say that uniform improvement in a small sample cannot prove

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:42.180
the symptom change was independent of weight loss and cannot be laid at Terzepetite's

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:49.493
door. Monocyte Messenger RNA for the GIP receptor is what a diabetology international paper measured

00:04:49.493 --> 00:04:55.193
in 90 people with type 2 diabetes at a single center. Each person had already been on a

00:04:55.193 --> 00:04:59.593
PLP1 receptor agonist for at least six months before a switch to tersepotide.

00:05:00.093 --> 00:05:05.113
Higher receptor message at baseline went with larger six-month drops in weight, and in

00:05:05.113 --> 00:05:09.633
the fibrosis-4 index, and both links held after multivariable adjustment.

00:05:10.293 --> 00:05:14.873
The fibrosis-4 link still held after the analysts accounted for how much weight was lost.

00:05:15.533 --> 00:05:19.873
That same message did not predict weight change during the earlier GLP1 period.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:26.553
fibrosis 4 is a calculated index from age and blood tests, a biomarker, not a biopsy

00:05:26.553 --> 00:05:28.153
and not a liver disease outcome.

00:05:28.693 --> 00:05:34.673
In exploratory dishes, native GIP damped the interleukin 6 and tumor necrosis factor alpha

00:05:34.673 --> 00:05:38.793
response, that bacterial lipopolysaccharide provoked in monocytes.

00:05:39.413 --> 00:05:42.433
The authors call the blood cell marker exploratory only.

00:05:42.953 --> 00:05:47.993
They did not show the association is specific to this switch, did not show the receptor cause

00:05:47.993 --> 00:05:51.713
the change, and did not show that scar tissue in the liver regressed.

00:05:52.622 --> 00:05:58.022
A sheep study suggests semi-glutide may lower fetal oxygen, which is animal evidence, not

00:05:58.022 --> 00:05:59.402
a finding in pregnant people.

00:06:00.022 --> 00:06:04.602
A study described by the Royal Australian College of General Practitioners and the University

00:06:04.602 --> 00:06:10.042
of Western Australia ties resistance training to less muscle loss and to muscle function held

00:06:10.042 --> 00:06:15.562
on to during GLP1 weight loss, without a design or an effect size in the reports at hand.

00:06:15.562 --> 00:06:21.102
Baylor College of Medicine's blog says a veteran's affairs trial will test GLP-1 medicines

00:06:21.102 --> 00:06:25.302
for alcohol use disorder in veterans, a plan rather than a result.

00:06:25.942 --> 00:06:31.602
UA.News, citing news medical, says 90% of eligible teens in the United States got neither

00:06:31.602 --> 00:06:33.802
surgery nor a GLP-1 drug.

00:06:34.869 --> 00:06:39.989
Terzepetide, the subject of this week's spotlight, is an assulated peptide built to switch on

00:06:39.989 --> 00:06:43.429
two receptors at once, GIP and GLP-1.

00:06:43.429 --> 00:06:49.189
and a 2022 review calls it the first dual agonist of that pair approved for type 2 diabetes

00:06:49.189 --> 00:06:51.929
in the United States, Europe and the UAE.

00:06:52.489 --> 00:06:58.789
The sequence is 39 amino acids, drawn from native GIP and altered so one molecule can engage

00:06:58.789 --> 00:06:59.669
both receptors.

00:07:00.289 --> 00:07:05.149
Those receptors help drive insulin release, and they also sit in brain regions that govern

00:07:05.149 --> 00:07:05.829
food intake.

00:07:06.489 --> 00:07:12.129
The reason anyone combined the two hormones is older human physiology summarized in a 2021

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:12.909
review.

00:07:13.429 --> 00:07:18.469
GIP alone, pushed to very high infusion levels, had not looked able to release insulin

00:07:18.469 --> 00:07:22.669
in people with type 2 diabetes, so it was shelved as a glucose drug.

00:07:23.129 --> 00:07:29.289
Infusing GLP1 and GIP together produced a larger insulin response and a stronger break on

00:07:29.289 --> 00:07:31.569
glucose than either hormone by itself.

00:07:32.129 --> 00:07:34.469
That is experimental physiology in people.

00:07:34.969 --> 00:07:40.469
Not a phase 3 outcomes trial, and it does not prove the GIP half is what adds benefit once

00:07:40.469 --> 00:07:46.469
both activities live in one weekly peptide. Five surpassed trials in people with type-2 diabetes

00:07:46.469 --> 00:07:54.329
are the strongest human evidence in these papers. HBA1C fell by 1.24 to 2.58 percentage points,

00:07:54.829 --> 00:08:02.369
and body weight fell by 5.4 to 11.7 kilograms. Ranges that review calls unprecedented for one agent.

00:08:02.969 --> 00:08:09.129
Between 23 and 62.4% of participants hit an HBA1C target the paper describes.

00:08:09.129 --> 00:08:15.229
types. Glucose and weight fell further than with semi-glutide, a GLP-1 only peptide, and

00:08:15.229 --> 00:08:20.509
further than with titrated basal insulin. Insulin sensitivity and the insulin secretory

00:08:20.509 --> 00:08:27.049
response improved more than with semi-glutide. Mealtime insulin and glucagon were lower. Apatite

00:08:27.049 --> 00:08:31.769
fell by a similar amount, and weight fell more, which means the extra weight loss is not

00:08:31.769 --> 00:08:34.929
explained only by the appetite change those trials recorded.

00:08:34.929 --> 00:08:41.709
A meta-analysis that searched through the 27th of October 2021, pooled 7 randomized trials

00:08:41.709 --> 00:08:46.989
lasting at least 12 weeks, 6,609 adults with type 2 diabetes.

00:08:47.649 --> 00:08:52.169
HBA-1C superiority was dose-dependent against every comparator class.

00:08:52.769 --> 00:08:58.709
Versus placebo, the mean gaps ran from 1.62 to 2.06 percentage points.

00:08:58.709 --> 00:09:07.149
Versus other GLP-1 receptor agonists, they ran from 0.29 to 0.92. Versus Basil Insulin

00:09:07.149 --> 00:09:16.149
they ran from 0.70 to 1.09. Extra weight loss versus GLP-1 drugs ran from 1.68 kg at

00:09:16.149 --> 00:09:22.969
the lowest dose in that pool to 7.16 at the highest. When that review was written, Terzepetide

00:09:22.969 --> 00:09:29.229
was still under review for approval. Use the 2022 paper for status, and the meta-analysis for

00:09:29.229 --> 00:09:34.849
the pooled comparisons. Heart data in the 2022 review are a safety check with few events.

00:09:35.509 --> 00:09:40.709
Adjudicators looked across the program, a four-part outcome, non-fatal heart attack,

00:09:41.029 --> 00:09:47.049
non-fatal stroke, cardiovascular death, and admission for angina tended to be lower over as

00:09:47.049 --> 00:09:52.909
long as about two years. In a program-wide meta-analysis, no cardiovascular outcome had

00:09:52.909 --> 00:09:58.409
a hazard ratio above one against pooled comparators, and the upper confidence bounds for major

00:09:58.409 --> 00:10:04.669
events sat under 1.3, which met a standard definition of cardiovascular safety. A ratio

00:10:04.669 --> 00:10:09.689
that has not risen above one on a small event count does not show that heart attacks are

00:10:09.689 --> 00:10:10.149
prevented.

00:10:10.149 --> 00:10:12.849
The harms look like GLP-1 harms.

00:10:13.249 --> 00:10:19.769
The 2022 review names nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and constipation, more often at higher doses.

00:10:20.409 --> 00:10:25.769
In the meta-analysis, low blood sugar was about as common as with placebo and less common

00:10:25.769 --> 00:10:27.009
than with basal insulin.

00:10:27.529 --> 00:10:32.949
Against placebo, nausea was more frequent, especially at the highest dose, with an odds ratio

00:10:32.949 --> 00:10:38.709
of 5.60, vomiting 5.50, and diarrhea 3.31.

00:10:38.709 --> 00:10:44.169
gut effects were generally similar to other GLP1 drugs, except diarrhea at the

00:10:44.169 --> 00:10:49.789
middle dose odds ratio 1.51. The highest dose led to more people leaving the study

00:10:49.789 --> 00:10:54.549
drug because of side effects, whichever comparator was used. Serious adverse

00:10:54.549 --> 00:10:59.069
events and deaths were not increased in that pool. What is still open is the claim

00:10:59.069 --> 00:11:05.269
people repeat most. The 2022 review says GIP cuts food intake and body weight in

00:11:05.269 --> 00:11:08.389
rodents, and that those effects have not been shown in humans.

00:11:08.949 --> 00:11:13.989
It also says nobody has yet shown that turning on the GIP receptor can improve insulin

00:11:13.989 --> 00:11:15.809
secretion in type 2 diabetes.

00:11:16.469 --> 00:11:19.269
A group earlier work found unresponsive to GIP.

00:11:19.829 --> 00:11:25.529
A larger drop in glucose and weight than with a GLP-1 only drug is a human trial result.

00:11:26.109 --> 00:11:28.929
A proven GIP explanation for that gap is not.

00:11:29.889 --> 00:11:34.609
Cardiovascular follow-up in these sources runs up to about two years, with few events.

00:11:34.609 --> 00:11:40.049
The papers do not show a longer horizon, do not show benefit outside type 2 diabetes,

00:11:40.609 --> 00:11:45.089
and do not convert a biomarker link or an uncontrolled clinic series into proof that

00:11:45.089 --> 00:11:47.089
the dual agonist caused those changes.

00:11:48.032 --> 00:11:52.372
One thing worth knowing from the clinic records is that heart events clustered among people

00:11:52.372 --> 00:11:56.892
who had stopped, while illness or other reasons for stopping can still explain the gap.

00:11:57.472 --> 00:12:02.572
A required eye warning is a regulator deciding a rare optic nerve event belongs on the label,

00:12:02.572 --> 00:12:05.632
level, which is not the same as a trial that counts the event.

00:12:06.172 --> 00:12:11.352
In randomized trials and thousands of adults with type 2 diabetes, the dual peptide lowered

00:12:11.352 --> 00:12:16.932
glucose and weight more than GLP1 only drugs and basal insulin, and the human share of

00:12:16.932 --> 00:12:19.832
that gap that belongs to GIP is still unproven.

00:12:20.412 --> 00:12:25.372
In a small clinic series without a control group, lipidema scores improved without tracking

00:12:25.372 --> 00:12:29.912
weight loss, and that improvement cannot be credited to the drug until a controlled study

00:12:29.912 --> 00:12:30.492
says so.

